wg-wrangler (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  Identical to 0.4.0~rc4. The entries below carry the detail; the headlines
  since 0.3.1 are:

  * Build targets are ubuntu 22.04, 24.04, 26.04, debian 12 and 13. All five are
    now also covered by the test suite, which used to run on two of them
  * Requires node 20 or newer and perl 5.34 or newer. configure used to accept
    perl 5.22 and silently skipped the frontend build on any node above 18
  * qooxdoo updated to 7.9.3, Net::IP replaced by the maintained Net::IP::XS
  * Two behaviour changes worth noting before upgrading: address validation now
    rejects input it used to accept, and 'Allowed IPs' is a required field for
    the first time. A typo there used to end up verbatim in the client
    configuration mailed to the peer
  * The maintainer scripts no longer fail when the wg-wrangler_manager account
    already exists as a regular user, and postrm no longer reverts permissions
    on every upgrade
  * Test suite grew from 36 to 96 tests

 -- Manuel Oetiker <manuel@oetiker.ch>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:05:36 +0200

wg-wrangler (0.4.0~rc4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Removed the name attributes from the action config of WireguardShow. Every
    start logged "action should not have a name attribute" once per worker.
    CallBackery overwrites the name of a popup action right after warning about
    it, so the attributes were never used for anything

 -- Manuel Oetiker <manuel@oetiker.ch>  Sat, 08 Aug 2026 16:18:26 +0200

wg-wrangler (0.4.0~rc3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed the maintainer scripts. postinst aborted when an account named
    wg-wrangler_manager already existed as a regular user, left the .gitconfig
    unwritten because the home directory was never created, and still exited 0,
    so dpkg considered the half configured package installed
  * postrm no longer runs on upgrade. It used to revert the group of
    /etc/wireguard, drop the sudoers rule and try to delete the account on every
    upgrade, relying on the incoming postinst to restore all of it
  * The sudoers rule is written instead of appended and gets mode 0440
  * Documented which account and home directory the package uses, and how to
    point an existing account at it. git reads the home directory from
    /etc/passwd, so a .gitconfig written elsewhere is never seen

 -- Manuel Oetiker <manuel@oetiker.ch>  Fri, 07 Aug 2026 17:26:50 +0200

wg-wrangler (0.4.0~rc2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * configure requires perl 5.34 instead of 5.22. Nothing below 5.34 was built
    or tested, 5.34 on ubuntu 22.04 is the oldest of the five build targets
  * Replaced debian/compat with debhelper-compat in Build-Depends. The file was
    itself deprecated and produced 74 warnings per package build
  * Added tests for WireguardDataAdapter, which had no coverage although it
    hosts the validator dispatch behind every peer form field. The suite is now
    at 96 tests

 -- Manuel Oetiker <manuel@oetiker.ch>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 13:58:54 +0200

wg-wrangler (0.4.0~rc1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Debian packages are built again, for debian 12 and 13 alongside ubuntu
    24.04 and 26.04
  * Replaced Net::IP, unmaintained since 2012, with Net::IP::XS
  * looks_like_ip() now actually validates. It discarded the parse result and
    accepted everything, so a typo in 'Allowed IPs' or 'DNS' went straight
    into the client configuration mailed to the peer. Empty values are
    rejected as well, which is what makes the required flag on 'allowed-ips'
    take effect for the first time
  * Added tests for the IPManager validation and error paths, raising branch
    coverage of that module from 40% to 81%

 -- Manuel Oetiker <manuel@oetiker.ch>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 08:59:49 +0200

wg-wrangler (0.4.0~beta) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Build targets are now ubuntu 24.04 and 26.04; the dead debian 10/11 and
    ubuntu 18.04/20.04 targets are gone
  * configure now accepts node 20 through 26 and requires at least 20. Before
    this it silently skipped the frontend build on anything newer than node 18
  * qooxdoo updated to 7.9.3
  * debhelper compat raised from the deprecated 9 to 13
  * GitHub actions updated; the unit test matrix had exclude rules that stopped
    it from ever testing node 22 on ubuntu 24.04
  * ubuntu 26.04 needs libnet-idn-encode-perl, since Net::IDN::Encode no longer
    compiles with gcc 15. It is a build and a runtime dependency
  * Fixed a race in thirdparty that let a parallel make run bin/cpanm while it
    was still being downloaded
  * Fixed the version rewrite rule, which replaced every dotted number triple in
    README.md and had repeatedly corrupted the example listen address and the
    cpanfile snapshot name

 -- Manuel Oetiker <manuel@oetiker.ch>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 17:24:07 +0200

